  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "When you submit your app for review, if itʼs approved and the status changes to Pending Developer Release, then you can release a version. For more information about app review, see `https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-submissions-to-app-review/submit-for-review`. For more information about manually releasing versions, see `https://devcms.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-your-apps-availability/select-a-version-release-option`. For more information about app status, see `https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/app-and-submission-statuses`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-submissions-to-app-review/submit-for-review",
            "https://devcms.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-your-apps-availability/select-a-version-release-option",
            "https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/app-and-submission-statuses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Important**\n>\n>  Send this request only when you’re ready to publish your version. You can’t cancel this request.",
